        "dependency_level": 1
      },
      {
        "id": "thm-benjamini-hochberg-independent-fdr",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "title": "Benjamini–Hochberg FDR under independence",
        "statement": "Let $\\mathsf E=((\\mathcal X,\\mathcal A),\\Theta,(P_\\theta)_{\\theta\\in\\Theta})$\nbe a statistical experiment, let $m\\ge1$, and fix a prespecified family of\nnonempty null hypotheses $H_{01},\\ldots,H_{0m}\\subseteq\\Theta$ with valid p-value\nstatistics $p_i:\\mathcal X\\to[0,1]$. For each $\\theta$, put\n\n$$I_0(\\theta)=\\{i:\\theta\\in H_{0i}\\},\\qquad m_0(\\theta)=|I_0(\\theta)|.$$\n\nSuppose that under every $P_\\theta$ the $m$ p-values are mutually independent\nand that\n\n$$P_\\theta\\{p_i(X)\\le u\\}=u\\qquad(i\\in I_0(\\theta),\\ 0\\le u\\le1).$$\n\nFalse-null p-value laws may otherwise be arbitrary. For every $q\\in(0,1)$,\nthe BH rule in [[alg-benjamini-hochberg-step-up-procedure]] satisfies\n\n$$\\operatorname{FDR}_\\theta=\\frac{m_0(\\theta)}{m}q\\le q.$$\n\nThis is an FDR guarantee; no FWER bound is asserted.",
        "deps": [
          "alg-benjamini-hochberg-step-up-procedure",
          "cor-expectation-linearity-monotonicity-and-modulus-bound",
          "cor-expectation-of-an-indicator-is-probability",
          "def-expectation-of-a-nonnegative-or-integrable-random-variable",
          "def-false-discovery-rate-and-familywise-error-rate",
          "def-independent-random-elements",
          "def-p-value",
          "lem-benjamini-hochberg-leave-one-out-identity",
          "thm-grouping-independent-sigma-algebras",
          "thm-independent-random-elements-have-product-joint-law"
        ],
