        "id": "ex-benjamini-hochberg-fdr-versus-fwer",
        "kind": "example",
        "title": "A two-test BH family distinguishes FDR from FWER",
        "statement": "Take two hypotheses and $q=1/2$. Under the specified law, $H_1$ is true with\n$P_1\\sim\\operatorname{Unif}[0,1]$, while $H_2$ is false with $P_2=0$ almost\nsurely. The p-values are independent. The BH procedure has\n$\\operatorname{FDR}=1/4$ and $\\operatorname{FWER}=1/2$, so its FDR bound is\nattained while FDR and FWER differ.",
